{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And it was, when Pharaoh hardened.</b> And since Pharaoh hardened himself against sending us forth — he being likened to a donkey, as it says: אֲשֶׁר בְּשַׂר חֲמוֹרִים בְּשָׂרָם (Ezekiel 23:20) — and he could have redeemed himself and his people by sending Israel forth, they being likened to a sheep, as it says: שֶׂה פְּזוּרָה יִשְׂרָאֵל (Jeremiah 50:17), and likewise as it says: וְאַתֵּנָה צֹאנִי (Ezekiel 34:31)." "<b>And HaShem killed.</b> And the El killed him who was likened to a donkey, since he was not redeemed by a sheep." "<b>Every firstborn in the land of Egypt.</b> The firstborn of Israel were liable to be struck together with them, on the principle of פֶּן תִּסָּפֶה בַּעֲוֹן הָעִיר (Genesis 19:15). He delivered them through that which He consecrated to Himself, so that the human firstborn of Israel were like Nazirites or more — set apart for the service of the blessed El, and forbidden for ordinary labor." "<b>Therefore I sacrifice.</b> The firstborn of the animal." "<b>And every firstborn of my sons I redeem.</b> So that they be permitted for ordinary (non-sacred) use."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:23.567112241Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}